.TH IMUD\-INFLUXDB.CONF 5 "2026-08-05" "imud 1.8.2" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
imud\-influxdb.conf \- configuration file for imud-influxdb(8)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/imud/imud-influxdb.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configuration for the
.BR imud-influxdb (8)
bridge daemon, which reads imud's binary stream socket and writes InfluxDB
line-protocol points over UDP and/or HTTP.  The daemon runs whenever
.B enabled
is true and stays healthy under systemd; each output
.RB ( udp_enabled ,\  http_enabled )
is independent and off by default, so nothing is written until you turn one on.
The bridge reads
.B only
this file (never
.IR imud.conf ).
The file is one
.B [imud-influxdb]
section of
.IR key " = " value
lines; strings are double-quoted and
.RB \(oq # \(cq
begins a comment.  Requires imud's
.B [stream]
output enabled.
.PP
Keys marked
.B [hot]
are reloaded on
.BR SIGHUP ;
keys marked
.B [restart]
take effect on the next service start.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B enabled
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ true )\ [restart]
Run the InfluxDB bridge daemon.  With it true and every output off the daemon
runs but writes nothing; set it false to not run the bridge at all (it exits
cleanly, so systemd does not restart it).
.TP
.B socket
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq/run/imud/imud-stream.sock\(dq )\ [restart]
imud stream socket to read.
.TP
.B transport
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq\(dq )\ [restart]
.B DEPRECATED.
Legacy output selector
.RB ( udp " or " http );
kept only for old configs.  When neither
.B udp_enabled
nor
.B http_enabled
is set, a
.B transport
value is mapped to the matching enable (with a warning).  Prefer the enables.
.TP
.B rate_hz
.RI ( int ,\ default:\ 10 )\ [hot]
Point emit rate in Hz; must be greater than zero.
.TP
.B measurement
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dqimud\(dq )\ [hot]
Line-protocol measurement name.
.TP
.B source_label
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dqimud\(dq )\ [hot]
Value of the
.B source=
tag.
.TP
.B units
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dqdeg\(dq )\ [hot]
.B deg
(degrees, \(de/min) or
.B rad
(SI: radians, rad/s).
.TP
.B publish_heave
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ true )\ [hot]
Include the
.B heave
field.
.TP
.B udp_enabled
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ false )\ [restart]
Write line-protocol points over UDP.
.TP
.B udp_addr
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq127.0.0.1\(dq )\ [hot]
UDP destination host (InfluxDB 1.x listener or Telegraf).
.TP
.B udp_port
.RI ( int ,\ default:\ 8089 )\ [hot]
UDP destination port.
.TP
.B http_enabled
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ false )\ [restart]
Write line-protocol points over HTTP (may run alongside
.BR udp_enabled ).
.TP
.B http_host
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq127.0.0.1\(dq )\ [restart]
HTTP host.
.TP
.B http_port
.RI ( int ,\ default:\ 8086 )\ [restart]
HTTP port.
.TP
.B http_path
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq/write?db=imud&precision=ns\(dq )\ [restart]
Write path: 1.x
.IR /write?db=<db> ,
or 2.x
.IR /api/v2/write?org=<org>&bucket=<bucket> ,
with
.BR precision=ns .
.TP
.B http_token
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq\(dq )\ [restart]
InfluxDB 2.x API token.  Stored in plaintext, which is why this file installs
mode 0640 owned
.IR root:imud .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud-influxdb.conf
This file.
Installed mode 0640, owner
.IR root:imud ,
because it can hold a plaintext API token: readable by root and by the
.I imud
user the bridge runs as, and by nobody else.
The bridge refuses to start if the file exists but cannot be read, rather than
falling back to defaults.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/imud-influxdb/examples/imud-influxdb.conf
Pristine template, mode 0644.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imud-influxdb (8),
.BR imud.conf (5),
.BR imud (8)
